{
  "id": "06034_tamerau",
  "headword": "{躊躇|ためら}う",
  "reading": "ためらう",
  "part_of_speech": "verb (godan)",
  "gloss": "to hesitate",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to hesitate, to waver, to falter",
      "explanation": "To be uncertain or reluctant to act, speak, or proceed due to doubt, fear, or indecision. Often used when one cannot make a decision or is afraid to take action."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "06034_tamerau_ex1",
      "japanese": "{彼|かれ}は{返事|へんじ}をためらった。",
      "english": "He hesitated to answer.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "06034_tamerau_ex2",
      "japanese": "ためらわずに{言|い}ってください。",
      "english": "Please don't hesitate to say it.",
      "notes": "Common expression using negative form",
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "06034_tamerau_ex3",
      "japanese": "{一瞬|いっしゅん}ためらってから、ドアを{開|あ}けた。",
      "english": "After hesitating for a moment, I opened the door.",
      "notes": "Shows the verb used with time expression",
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    }
  ],
  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY: {自動詞|じどうし} (intransitive). No pair verb. Often takes the pattern ～するのをためらう (hesitate to do ~).\n\nASPECT: ている indicates ongoing state of indecision. ためらっている = 'is hesitating' or 'is wavering.'\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n・{返事|へんじ}をためらう (hesitate to answer)\n・{決断|けつだん}をためらう (hesitate to make a decision)\n・ためらわずに (without hesitation)\n・ためらいがちに (hesitantly)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS: {迷|まよ}う focuses on being lost or confused about choices, while ためらう emphasizes reluctance or wavering before action.",
